{"abstract":"Music and composition by Montes_ea (Thomas Ahlmark & Kristoffer Jørgensen) Visuals and animation by Michelle & Uri Kranot Supported by: The Animation Workshop / VIA University college, VIA Design & Business, Viborg UNESCO Media Arts City, Kulturelt Samråd Herning, Koda Kultur, Bogtrykmuseet Vingaards Officin, Aarhus University Herbarium, Phenomenal Viborg","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kranot, Michelle","Kranot, Uriel","Ahlmark, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-660587"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["aesthetics design and media"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"garden alchemy av viborg an immersive audiovisual journey","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-660587","ids":["via-c9b00503-1d2a-4f61-ab4c-2607329ffa3c"],"keyword":["aesthetics, design and media"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-6A35760A930EA1EE2EE5F5DB60CD6DF3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Animated Culture","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Expanded Animation","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotmichellepau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uriel","key":"kranoturielpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"7413029c-0fee-4177-b1f6-8f9e384e8ff9","name":"Kranot, Uriel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"ahlmarkthomaspau","last":"Ahlmark","locid":"7b618da2-03d9-43ad-b4c3-aeaa3cd85e5e","name":"Ahlmark, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Viborg Paletten","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-c9b00503-1d2a-4f61-ab4c-2607329ffa3c"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Garden Alchemy AV Viborg : An immersive audiovisual journey","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-660587","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"(Original titel in Danish: Stedet Fortælling: undersøgt gennem håndtegning og animation) The workshop Site Stories challenged the traditional technical-engineering and more factual understanding of the materiality of an urban space with an artistic, fictional, and bodily-sensual perspective! With the aim of engendering a poetic and imaginative sense of place we encouraged bachelor students in architecture and urban design to pay extra attention to the stories revealed in surfaces and details in a number of selected urban spaces and historical building sites. The pedagogical purpose of the workshop was to teach students to start experimenting with their understanding of materiality, and to begin to fantasize about how humans are sentient bodies and narrative beings, as well as to strengthen students’ future understanding of how to design urban spaces. But – importantly – we also aimed to provide a space for students to make their own surprising discoveries and explorations on site thinking, to delve into different drawing techniques and to discover the potential of animation as a valuable design tool in the creative design process. Inspired by the books Site-writing: The Architecture of Art Criticism and The Architecture of Psychoanalysis: Spaces of Transition written by our guest lecturer; Professor Jane Rendell from the Bartlett School of Architecture (UCL) in England, the overall structure of the workshop was divided into five phases: 1) The Material, 2) The Emotional, 3) The Remembered, 4) The Dreamed, and 5) The Imagined. The first two phases focused on drawing techniques. Here students explored working with smaller drawing paper and vignettes, with paper larger than themselves and frottage, as well as with different retelling opportunities through bricolage and collage. In the final three phases, students worked with animation. With the help of the two award-winning animators; Michelle Kranot and Uriel Kranot leaders of the ANIDOX at the Center for Animation, Vizualization, and Digital Storytelling at VIA University College in Denmark, our students reinterpreted ways of telling and analysing an urban site. In the end, all the drawing explorations and animations were collected to create a joint exhibition and booklet.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Tvedebrink, Tenna Doktor Olsen","Olsen, Tina Vestermann","Rendell, Jane","Smith, Shelley Robin","Kranot, Michelle","Kranot, Uriel Shimon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-101513"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University College London"],"keyword":["Animation","Drawing","Education","Urban Architecture","Workshop"],"level":"edu","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Independent Researcher"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"site stories explorations of urban spaces through drawing and animation 000000000025 000000000029 april 000000002022","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","text":"Undefined","type":"url","url":"https://site-writing.co.uk/site-stories-explorations-of-urban-spaces-through-drawing-and-animation-25-29-april-2022/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-101513","ids":["aau-b1523338-0152-45ff-ae07-9ab6a2646db1"],"keyword":["Animation","Drawing","Education","Site Stories","Urban Architecture","Workshop"],"lang":"English","level":"Educational","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7FF819D7C9A8CEA16354425A6BA555DC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Brain, Body, Architecture Research","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Create Integrated Architecture","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Architecture and Urban Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Sustainable Architecture – SARC"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university college london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University College London","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Independent Researcher"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA University College"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tenna Doktor Olsen","key":"tvedebrinktennadoktorolsenpau","last":"Tvedebrink","locid":"cf3d8623-79f6-43b9-af59-9d36f0969cce","name":"Tvedebrink, Tenna Doktor Olsen","orcid":"0000-0002-6183-3888","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tina Vestermann","key":"olsentinavestermannpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"b957050b-0693-4b1d-b26b-101baab3c472","name":"Olsen, Tina Vestermann","orcid":"0000-0001-6281-7495","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane","key":"rendelljaneped","last":"Rendell","name":"Rendell, Jane","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Shelley Robin","key":"smithshelleyrobinoth","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Shelley Robin","rank":4,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotmichelleoth","last":"Kranot","name":"Kranot, Michelle","rank":5,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Uriel Shimon","key":"kranoturielshimonoth","last":"Kranot","name":"Kranot, Uriel Shimon","rank":6,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["aau-b1523338-0152-45ff-ae07-9ab6a2646db1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Site Stories: explorations of urban spaces through drawing and animation (25-29 April 2022)","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-101513","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Helsingor Kulturværftet presents: The concept of home is the key – you are home, but it is not your home. The notion of returning home to the forced intimacy of a hybrid space which is both public and domestic at once, allows us to transcend the narrative and character driven dramaturgy. We Are at Home is a playful and captivating multi-user installation focused on technology-mediated social interactions: VR frees us to experiment with form, space, and immersive environments, where the layered dramaturgy, physicality, and interactivity suggest an internal language of storytelling. Visually, and story-wise, the participant’s journey is affected because they are a part of a group – the experience peaks with a call for action: no longer theatrical or observational, it becomes a moral question of who will take action, who will follow, and who will resist.  And that changes everything. “We Are at Home” has been written, directed and designed by Michelle & Uri Kranot and co-producered by Danish Late Love Production, French Miyu Productions and Floréal Films as well as National Film Board of Canada.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kranot, Michelle","Kranot, Uriel","Nikolic, Lana Tankosa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-657512"],"event":{"end":"2022-11-17","place":"Helsingor, dk","start":"2022-08-15","title":"We Are at Home - CLICK / Kulturværftet","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["aesthetics design and media","technology engineering and IT"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"we are at home helsingor kulturværftet vr multiuser installation","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-657512","ids":["via-5ceb2fc7-1b39-438a-835d-8ab58a03fd34"],"keyword":["aesthetics, design and media","technology, engineering and IT"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-533893D8C34693E07E70EA3F69582033"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotmichellepau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uriel","key":"kranoturielpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"7413029c-0fee-4177-b1f6-8f9e384e8ff9","name":"Kranot, Uriel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lana Tankosa","key":"nikoliclanatankosappu","last":"Nikolic","locid":"91a1b46c-374b-4368-84af-52e4cb0892a6","name":"Nikolic, Lana Tankosa","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-5ceb2fc7-1b39-438a-835d-8ab58a03fd34"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"We Are at Home - Helsingor Kulturværftet : VR multiuser Installation","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-657512","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The Microgravity Slope Based on the question - How can we share the experience of an alternate gravity? We led a series of experiments that revealed multiple layers of communication, immersion, and choreographic setups and weaved together performance, participation, and spectatorship into a form we call Action Performance. The story of becoming an astronaut and exploring the solar system was introduced as a method to ignite the imagination and bodily engagement. It gradually became a core topic in the research, together with the fabrication of microgravity (moonlike gravity) through a harness based vertical dance system. In the past three years, cross disciplinary meetings and explorations with artists from the field of dance, Virtual Reality, animation and sound, lead to evolving participatory choreographies that took place in residencies at Åbne Scene in Godsbanen (2020 & 2022) and as part of the MFA thesis project Tiny Astronauts - Looking for Awe and Wonder finding Curiosity (June 2021). The most recent exploration named Microgravity is supported by the Danish Arts Council and The Animation Workshop, where we developed a VR environment and technology meant to challenge the boundaries and scale for moving vertically in space. We observed that curiosity is the most activating component of awe and wonder and that immersive storytelling can go hand in hand with bodily curiosity and learning. Here the concept of Expanded Choreography, we see as an invitation to re-look at physical experiences from the subjective point of view as choreographic, and as an opportunity to let the body and senses lead a reflecting process. Finally, as the topic of space travel became more significant and present, we also arrived at a follow-up question aimed at future research: Can empathy be practiced and present as part of our research? The core artist team consists of Esther Wrobel, Michelle Kranot, Tanya Rydell Montan, Lucia Jaen Serrano and Yann Coppier.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Worbel, Esther","Kranot, Michelle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-656067"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-08","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2022-07-05","title":"15th NOFOD Nordic Dance Forum conference, Copenhagen 5-8 July 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Research designs theory and method","aesthetics design and media","children and youth"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Sparrow Dance"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the microgravity slope cross disciplinary meetings and explorations with artists from the field of dance virtual reality animation and sound","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-656067","ids":["via-29cd8fcc-e20b-4ab7-b9a5-52a9e8ff05db"],"keyword":["aesthetics, design and media","children and youth","research designs, theory and method"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2C4E17E03B6A925C66FAB59F09F42678"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Sparrow Dance"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Esther","key":"worbelpau","last":"Worbel","name":"Worbel, Esther","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-29cd8fcc-e20b-4ab7-b9a5-52a9e8ff05db"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"The Microgravity Slope : Cross disciplinary meetings and explorations with artists from the field of dance, Virtual Reality, animation and sound","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-656067","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"At THIS 2022, we invite you to try a multi-awarded VR experience in immersive storytelling. Inspired by the 1922 Carl Sandburg poem of the same title, this VR single-user immersive experience explores themes of acknowledgement and participation. It is not about hanging people, but about the awkward intimacy that comes with being human, and the connection between spectator, witness, and accomplice. Together with our VR host, you’ll get a chance to try out the experience and let yourself immerse into the universe of creative storytelling. The experience will take place during THIS 2022 in all three days of the festival.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kranot, Uriel","Kranot, Michelle","Nikolic, Lana Tankosa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-657752"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Innovation","Ledelse organisationsudvikling og innovation","Medier kommunikation og sprog","Teknik ingeniørvidenskab og IT","VR","Æstetik design og medier"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Late Love Production"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the hangman at home this aarhus vr single user installation","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-657752","ids":["via-65d30469-463a-4a95-a833-2aa7ade0fb00"],"keyword":["Ledelse, organisationsudvikling og innovation","Medier, kommunikation og sprog","Teknik, ingeniørvidenskab og IT","innovation","vr","Æstetik, design og medier"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7502C7A72BA35B0CA931B9F45AB085FB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Late Love Production"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uriel","key":"kranoturielpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"7413029c-0fee-4177-b1f6-8f9e384e8ff9","name":"Kranot, Uriel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotmichellepau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lana Tankosa","key":"nikoliclanatankosapau","last":"Nikolic","locid":"91a1b46c-374b-4368-84af-52e4cb0892a6","name":"Nikolic, Lana Tankosa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-65d30469-463a-4a95-a833-2aa7ade0fb00"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"The Hangman at Home - THIS Aarhus : VR Single User Installation","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-657752","year":"2022","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"By testing the frontiers of immersive art and moving images, and activating participation in location-based XR experiences, we are compelled to ask how the medium is changing the way we tell a story, and how animation is used to both excite and provoke. While much research on immersive storytelling focuses on theories and on audience experiences, as researchers at The Animation Workshop at the VIA University College Research & Development Department, our focus is on an investigation of the story design process through collaboration and shared experiences. The presentation will outline key case studies: from Nothing Happens (2017), Songbird (2018), The Hangman at Home (2021) and We Are at Home (2022), to the most current work-in-progress.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Kranot, Michelle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-659238"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-11","place":"Linz, at","start":"2022-09-07","title":"Ars Electronica","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Research designs theory and method","aesthetics design and media"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"michelle kranot expanded animation a focus on collaborative processes","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p8gPXtvxGsc&list=PLVCkZFJ5bLALLAyoBH7jN_5L-XqkdVgKy&index=4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-659238","ids":["via-99740ad1-92ef-419c-9314-bad8fc94fe03"],"keyword":["aesthetics, design and media","research designs, theory and method"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-523055E4340E13ACB58AAECC92A0BD1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=p8gPXtvxGsc&list=PLVCkZFJ5bLALLAyoBH7jN_5L-XqkdVgKy&index=4","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-99740ad1-92ef-419c-9314-bad8fc94fe03"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Michelle Kranot: Expanded Animation : A focus on Collaborative Processes","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-659238","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"‘We Are at Home’ is an immersive multi-user installation exploring themes of acknowledgement, participation and the awkward intimacy that comes with being human. “What does the hangman think about when he goes home at night from work?”. Inspired by the iconic Carl Sandburg poem (1922), this VR experience explores themes of acknowledgement and participation. It is not about hanging people, but about the awkward intimacy of being human, as well as the connection between observer, spectator, and accomplice. The animated, immersive experience invites you into five interwoven stories, capturing pivotal moments. “We Are at Home” ultimately reveals that we are all more alike than different, while raising questions of responsibility.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kranot, Uriel","Kranot, Michelle","Nikolic, Lana Tankosa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-660921"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Innovation","Media communication and languages","VR","aesthetics design and media","technology engineering and IT"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Late Love Production"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"we are at home cph dox vr multi user installation","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-660921","ids":["via-d62ddf8a-e998-4892-b7c2-9ca2cacae637"],"keyword":["Media, communication and languages","aesthetics, design and media","innovation","technology, engineering and IT","vr"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F2FDD755C640C1D45665B1D2D5311EB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Late Love Production"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uriel","key":"kranoturielpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"7413029c-0fee-4177-b1f6-8f9e384e8ff9","name":"Kranot, Uriel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotmichellepau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lana Tankosa","key":"nikoliclanatankosapau","last":"Nikolic","locid":"91a1b46c-374b-4368-84af-52e4cb0892a6","name":"Nikolic, Lana Tankosa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-d62ddf8a-e998-4892-b7c2-9ca2cacae637"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"We Are at Home - CPH DOX : VR Multi User Installation","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-660921","year":"2022","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Under the heading “Planet VR”, Nikolaj Kunsthal presents in the period 20–31 August a small handful of works that are significant and commendable in their own right in relation to the development of immersive VR experiences: What does the hangman think about when he walks home from work at night? “We Are at Home” (2021) is a multi-user virtual reality experience that explores the awkward intimacy of being human. Inspired by Carl Sandburg’s iconic poem from 1922, this VR experience explores themes of recognition and participation. It’s not about hanging people but about the awkward intimacy of being human as well as the connection being an observer, a witness and an accomplice. The animated and immersive experience invites you into five interwoven stories that capture decisive moments in the lives of five people. \"We Are at Home\" reveals that we humans have far more in common than you would expect. “We Are at Home” has been written, directed and designed by Michelle & Uri Kranot and co-producered by Danish Late Love Production, French Miyu Productions and Floréal Films as well as National Film Board of Canada.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kranot, Michelle","Kranot, Uriel","Nikolic, Lana Tankosa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-660026"],"event":{"end":"2022-08-31","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2022-08-20","title":"Planet VR","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["aesthetics design and media","technology engineering and IT"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"we are at home nikolaj kunsthal vr multiuser installation","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-660026","ids":["via-b51115e2-ecfa-42ea-8f55-c5e171800eed"],"keyword":["aesthetics, design and media","technology, engineering and IT"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-89FFAE71B7B8F98E437F9BB118A371D4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotmichellepau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uriel","key":"kranoturielpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"7413029c-0fee-4177-b1f6-8f9e384e8ff9","name":"Kranot, Uriel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lana Tankosa","key":"nikoliclanatankosappu","last":"Nikolic","locid":"91a1b46c-374b-4368-84af-52e4cb0892a6","name":"Nikolic, Lana Tankosa","rank":3,"role":"Publisher","rolecode":"ppu"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-b51115e2-ecfa-42ea-8f55-c5e171800eed"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"We Are at Home - Nikolaj Kunsthal : VR multiuser Installation","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-660026","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We are at Home er en immersiv oplevelse som udforsker temaer omkring anerkendelse og deltagelse og den akavede intimitet der er ved at være et menneske. Inspireret af Carl Sandburgs ikoniske digt fra 1922, udforsker denne VR-oplevelse temaer omkring anerkendelse og deltagelse. Det handler ikke om at hænge mennesker, men om den akavede intimitet der er ved at være et menneske, såvel som forbindelsen mellem at være iagttager, vidne og medskyldig. Den animerede fordybende (immersive) oplevelse inviterer ind til fem sammenvævede historier, som fanger afgørende øjeblikke i fem menneskers liv. We are at Home afslører at vi har langt mere tilfælles end som så og stiller spørgsmål om medansvar. Multi-user VR-oplevelsen begynder med en opfordring til handling, idet deltagerne bliver opfordret til at tænde en tændstik, hvilket udløser oplevelsen. Denne non-lineære flerlagede fortælling er både interaktiv og observatorisk. Brugerne får muligheden for at krydse forskellige tærskler; en dør, et vindue eller en pejs – som hver repræsenterer en portal ind til et rum, hvor én af de animerede scener udfolder sig. Brugerne får mulighed for at interagere med genstande, som er udvundet fra historierne, blive inddraget og skabe lydbilleder. Endelig opfordres man under denne tankevækkende, ofte legende rejse, til at deltage i et poetisk højdepunkt, hvor man vil opleve et kollektivt medansvar. We are at Home er et multi-medieprojekt der eksisterer som single-user VR-installation samt en stærk animeret kortfilm The Hangman at Home. We Are at Home havde sin internationale premiere i Tribeca og vandt ”Grand Prize Masque d’Or” i XR-konkurrencen i New Images Festival i Frankrig. Det er en koproduktion mellem Viborg-baserede Late Love Production (DK), Miyu Productions (Frankrig), Floréal Films (Frankrig) og National Film Board of Canada.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kranot, Uriel","Kranot, Michelle","Nikolic, Lana Tankosa"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-661672"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Innovation","Media communication and languages","VR","aesthetics design and media","management organizational development and innovation","technology engineering and IT"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-UC"],"level3":{"OT":["Late Love Production"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"we are at home phenomenal viborg vr multi user installation","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dnt","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-661672","ids":["via-f058da95-c872-49c8-9ae9-ab118cd359b4"],"keyword":["Media, communication and languages","aesthetics, design and media","innovation","management, organizational development and innovation","technology, engineering and IT","vr"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AF9B68836AB5EC8518FC71731FFB0177"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Late Love Production"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uriel","key":"kranoturielpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"7413029c-0fee-4177-b1f6-8f9e384e8ff9","name":"Kranot, Uriel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotmichellepau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lana Tankosa","key":"nikoliclanatankosapau","last":"Nikolic","locid":"91a1b46c-374b-4368-84af-52e4cb0892a6","name":"Nikolic, Lana Tankosa","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-f058da95-c872-49c8-9ae9-ab118cd359b4"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"We Are at Home - Phenomenal Viborg : VR Multi User Installation","type":"Non-Textual Item","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-661672","year":"2022","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The upheaval of the global COVID pandemic has likely transformed the traditional festival circuit as well as the way we watch films, consume content, and participate in events. Film festivals provide the independent animator and filmmaker opportunities to connect with audiences, develop networks, link with funders, producers, distributors and multipliers, usually with ‘face to face’ opportunities such as roundtables, pitching etc. In the absence of physical meetings, cinema experiences, and opportunities for live audience participation what are the challenges independent animation filmmakers face? Also, as new online platforms and solutions emerge, what does the new model look like? This post will summarise some of the key findings from the Indie Online research project led by Michelle Kranot of The Animation Workshop/VIA University College, and offers some suggestions for festivals and independent animators when considering new distribution models. The research took place between March 2020 and October 2020 and involved semi-structured interviews with 20 film festivals and 20 independent animators and filmmakers. The majority of interviewees reflected on the accessibility of the online format of a festival concluding that audiences (including filmmakers, distributors, multipliers, and the general public) can find the online format difficult to navigate and that film festivals need to invest more attention in helping them locate for the most valuable experience. The audiences’ physical appearance at a physical festival enables a navigation of the exhibition space(s) that is hard to replicate online. The screen can flatten and homogenize the audience’s experience.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Kranot, Michelle","Land, Ellie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-661745"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Northumbria University"],"keyword":["information and communication technologies and e learning"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a short summery of indie online adapting to new online platforms","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://blog.animationstudies.org/?p=4121","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-661745","ids":["via-f390bda7-f126-4087-8c66-f74e5b3ae77b"],"keyword":["information and communication technologies and e-learning"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-72B74F8CAE065F32271C1896C904E61F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://blog.animationstudies.org/?p=4121","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"northumbria university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Northumbria University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ellie","key":"landpau","last":"Land","name":"Land, Ellie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-f390bda7-f126-4087-8c66-f74e5b3ae77b"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"A short summery of Indie Online : Adapting to New Online Platforms","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-661745","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Acclaimed artists and filmmakers Michelle and Uri Kranot – whose previous experience with multimedia filmmaking and conceptually progressive storytelling includes the multi-award-winning projects Hollow Land, How Long Not Long, Nothing Happens and Songbird – have again combined their efforts for another thought-provoking and beautifully rendered animation piece. Taking the form of three distinct outputs that will be participating in a variety of festivals this summer, The Hangman At Home exists as a short film (premiering this week at the Krakow Film Festival), a single-user VR experience (part of this month’s Annecy Festival and International Film Festival Rotterdam programmes) as well as a multi-user VR performance and installation We Are At Home that will see its premiere at the Tribeca Film Festival next week. While each offers their own unique experience, they are conceptually linked by themes of intimacy, complicity, voyeurism and participation as the audience finds themselves alternately looking-in on, interacting with and occupying the personal spaces of a succession of strangers during their private moments. Taking inspiration from the 1922 Carl Sandburg poem of the same name, the scenarios that play out conjure a variety of emotions and personal reflections as regards our own habits, curiosities and social responsibilities as both audience member and participant of the world at large. The Hangman At Home/We Are At Home is internationally co-produced by Lana Tankosa Nikolic of Late Love Productions in Denmark, Katayoun Dibamehr and Avi Amar of Floréal Films in France, Emmanuel-Alain Raynal and Pierre Baussaron of MIYU Production (France), Marc Bertrand and Julie Roy of The National Film Board of Canada. In anticipation of the busy month ahead for all three outputs we were enthusiastic to catch up with Michelle Kranot about the thematic driving forces behind the project, the processes behind its stunning overall look and her work in supporting similarly ambitious new work as producer and creative director of The Animation Workshop’s creative development platform ANIDOX.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Mitchel, Ben","Kranot, Michelle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-659879"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Skwigly Online Animation Magazine"],"keyword":["Animation","VR","aesthetics design and media"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interview with michelle kranot the hangman at home we are at home","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"doo","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.skwigly.co.uk/michelle-kranot-hangman-at-home/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-659879","ids":["via-b042dcf0-82d8-44fd-89ae-def31e91e5a9"],"keyword":["Animation","VR","aesthetics, design and media","magazine"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E26821515141ED650BB082503E337568"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.skwigly.co.uk/michelle-kranot-hangman-at-home/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"skwigly online animation magazine","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Skwigly Online Animation Magazine","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Kreative erhverv og professioner","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, Center for animation, visualisering og digital fortælling","VIA, Uddannelser, Storytelling-, design- og businessuddannelserne, The Animation Workshop"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ben","key":"mitchelpau","last":"Mitchel","name":"Mitchel, Ben","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Michelle","key":"kranotpau","last":"Kranot","locid":"387ef20d-3bd4-4a0c-968b-c0abe0f9b7ad","name":"Kranot, Michelle","orcid":"0009-0003-1941-6014","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-b042dcf0-82d8-44fd-89ae-def31e91e5a9"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Interview with Michelle Kranot (The Hangman at Home | We Are at Home)","type":"Other-Unknown","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-659879","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
